<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Greencore says yr pretax profit up 16 pct.</title>
<headline>Greencore says yr pretax profit up 16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 30.</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)	     25.35		   vs 22.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	4.5		     vs 7.7</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)6.8		     vs.11.8</p>
<p> Pretax profit	   54.62		   vs 47.03</p>
<p> Turnover		 459.0		    vs 436.89</p>
<p>Operating profit before</p>
<p>exceptional item	  49.93		  vs 45.21</p>
<p> Exceptional item	 0.81 charge	  vs 1.14 credit</p>
<p> Interest received	5.02		   vs 2.79</p>
<p> Interest paid	    4.85		   vs 5.46</p>
<p> Tax charge		 7.91		   vs 7.47</p>
<p> Net taxed		  46.72		  vs 39.56</p>
<p> Attributable	     46.24		  vs 38.86</p>
<p> Registration date	December 24</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 17, 1997</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date	 December 16</p>
<p>NOTE - Irish-based food company Greencore Group Plc said the figures were adjusted to take account of its one-for-one share split in March 1996. It said overall the group continued to trade in line with expectations.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
